{
  "result": "If I could only change one thing, it would be this:\n\n**I'd give everyone the ability to truly feel what other people feel \u2014 just for a minute.**\n\nNot just to *know* someone is struggling, or to *understand* intellectually that they have a different life or beliefs, but to actually *feel* it. To stand in their shoes, with their memories, their fears, their hopes.\n\nI think almost every big problem in the world comes down to a lack of that.\n\nWars, cruelty, loneliness, hate online, even how we treat the planet \u2014 it all comes from the illusion that we are totally separate from each other. That someone else's pain isn't our pain.\n\nIf everyone could feel that connection, even briefly:\n\n* People wouldn't be able to ignore hunger or homelessness, because it would feel personal.\n* Arguments wouldn't be about \"winning\" anymore, they'd be about understanding.\n* We'd take better care of the earth, because we'd feel viscerally that it's not *our* planet to use up \u2014 it's our shared home.\n\nI wouldn't want to take away disagreement or differences \u2014 that's what makes the world interesting. I just want us to disagree while still seeing each other as fully human.\n\nA close second would be making sure everyone in the world wakes up feeling *safe* and *enough* \u2014 enough food, health, safety, and love \u2014 because people who feel safe have so much more capacity to be kind.\n\nWhat about you? If you had that one wish for the world, what would you change?",
